        "subject": "Biology",
        "chapter": "Tissues, Organs and Organ Systems",
        "chapterNumber": 4,
        "topic": "Plant Ground Tissues",
        "question": "Which simple permanent plant tissue is characterized by dead, uniformly thickened, highly lignified secondary walls that provide rigid mechanical strength to mature stems and nutshells?",
        "options": {
          "A": "Sclerenchyma",
          "B": "Parenchyma",
          "C": "Collenchyma",
          "D": "Chlorenchyma"
        },
        "correctAnswer": "A",
        "explanation": "Sclerenchyma cells (fibers and sclereids) are dead at maturity with thick, lignified secondary walls specialized for providing structural support and hardness.",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "verified": true,
        "source": "curriculum-bank",
