        "chapter": "Tissues, Organs and Organ Systems",
        "chapterNumber": 4,
        "topic": "Muscle Tissues",
        "question": "Which type of muscle tissue is striated, involuntary, branched, and possesses specialized intercalated discs for rapid electrical synchronization?",
        "options": {
          "A": "Cardiac muscle",
          "B": "Skeletal muscle",
          "C": "Smooth muscle",
          "D": "Visceral muscle"
        },
        "correctAnswer": "A",
        "explanation": "Cardiac muscle (in the myocardium) is striated, branched, uninucleate, and connected via intercalated discs containing gap junctions for synchronous contraction.",
        "difficulty": "medium",
