        "chapterNumber": 4,
        "topic": "Connective Tissues",
        "question": "Which connective tissue cells reside within small cavities called lacunae in a firm, flexible, rubbery chondroitin matrix devoid of direct blood vessels?",
        "options": {
          "A": "Chondrocytes (Cartilage cells)",
          "B": "Osteocytes (Bone cells)",
          "C": "Erythrocytes",
          "D": "Myocytes"
        },
        "correctAnswer": "A",
        "explanation": "Chondrocytes are the mature cells of cartilage, situated inside lacunae within an avascular, flexible collagenous matrix.",
        "difficulty": "hard",
