        "topic": "Plant Phloem Tissue",
        "question": "In angiosperm phloem tissue, which specialized living cell type lacks a nucleus at maturity and conducts organic food solutions, supported metabolically by an adjacent companion cell?",
        "options": {
          "A": "Sieve tube element",
          "B": "Tracheid",
          "C": "Vessel element",
          "D": "Xylem parenchyma"
        },
        "correctAnswer": "A",
        "explanation": "Sieve tube elements lose their nuclei and vacuoles at maturity to facilitate bulk flow of sugars, relying on adjoining nucleated companion cells for metabolic functions.",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "verified": true,
        "source": "curriculum-bank",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-23T18:00:00.000Z"
